1. WHAT THIS COVERS

   "the Software" means the PRISM robotics-operations platform in this
   repository and every artefact generated from it, including but not limited
   to:

   (a) the single-file frontend application `PRISM-v10-complete.html`, its
       service worker, manifest, and the public landing page `landing.html`;
   (b) the `prism-server` backend — source, database schema, migrations, and
       configuration;
   (c) the PRISM Cortex model artefacts (`*.onnx`, tokenizer, labels, ledger),
       the datasets and registry they are compiled from, and the trained
       weights themselves;
   (d) the product's data models and calibrated content, including the
       platform and payload catalogues, the task/technology tables and their
       modelled value figures, the compliance rulesets, the incident
       playbooks, and the verified use-case library;
   (e) the documentation, design standards, and specifications in this
       repository.

   Third-party components redistributed alongside the Software are NOT covered
   by this licence and remain under their own terms. See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

2. RESERVATION OF RIGHTS

   All rights are reserved. No licence, express or implied, is granted by
   publication, by the source being readable in a browser, or by any repository
   being publicly visible.

   Publishing a public demonstration build (see Section 4) is a limited act of
   publication for evaluation purposes. It is not a dedication to the public
   domain, not an open-source release, and not a waiver of any right.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Without the prior written permission of the copyright holder, you may not:

   (a) copy, reproduce, or redistribute the Software or any substantial part
       of it, in source or compiled form;
   (b) create derivative works, adaptations, ports, or translations;
   (c) use the Software, or any part of it, to build, train, evaluate, or
       fine-tune a machine-learning model, or include it in any dataset used
       for that purpose;
   (d) use the Software commercially, or operate it as a service;
   (e) sell, sublicence, rent, lease, or otherwise transfer any interest in it;
   (f) remove, obscure, or alter any copyright, licence, or attribution notice;
   (g) circumvent any technical measure that gates access to a feature, tier,
       or tenant.

   Clause (c) is stated explicitly because automated ingestion is the most
   likely way this work is copied at scale, and silence on the point is
   sometimes read as permission.

4. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   You may:

   (a) view and read the publicly published demonstration build, and run it in
       your own browser, for the sole purpose of evaluating PRISM;
   (b) quote short excerpts for commentary, review, journalism, teaching, or
       research, with attribution — where such use is permitted by the
       applicable copyright exception (fair dealing, fair use, or the local
       equivalent). This licence neither grants nor removes those exceptions;
   (c) exercise any right that cannot lawfully be restricted in your
       jurisdiction.

   Reading the published demonstration build does not grant permission to
   reimplement it. Ideas and functionality are not protected by copyright;
   the specific expression in this repository is.

